icit gradient differentiation API' refers to the differentiable / functional-optimizer category (often labelled Meta in TorchOpt terminology); exact symbol deferred to U1.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"A1: standard autograd means loss.backward(create_graph=False) plus optim.step(); create_graph=True is a control arm, not the comparator.</item>\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"U6: Should the primary measurement pin to a single thread (deterministic) or use all 24 cores (realistic)?\",\"$text\":\"U5: Is OS-peak RSS or tracemalloc peak the primary memory metric when they disagree on allocator reuse?</item>\"},\"$text\":\"U4: Is the full factorial of approximately 28.8k timed runs acceptable, or should cells (kappa sweep, seed count R=30) be pruned?</item>\"},\"$text\":\"U3: Which numerical-stability metric is primary: lower cross-seed loss variance, lower perturbation sensitivity, better convergence on ill-conditioned losses, or fp32-vs-fp64 gradient consistency?</item>\"},\"$text\":\"U2: Does the question emphasize single-step intermediate-data reuse, or meta-learning inner-outer differentiation through the optimizer?</item>\"},\"$text\":\"U1: Which exact TorchOpt API symbol(s) does the 'explicit gradient differentiation API' refer to?</item>\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-5c44362a-ea98-4ebd-899d-ff68525f1d75", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 24}
